---
model: gemini-3.5-flash
input:
  schema:
    clause_text: string
    clause_type: string
    section_number: string
    page_number: number
output:
  schema:
    obligations:
      type: array
      items:
        type: object
        properties:
          party: { type: string, enum: ["Customer", "Vendor"] }
          internal_owner: { type: string, enum: ["Operations", "Procurement", "Finance", "Legal", "Contract Manager"] }
          action: { type: string }
          obligation_type: { type: string, enum: ["EXPLICIT", "DERIVED", "AMBIGUOUS"] }
          frequency: { type: string, enum: ["ONE_TIME", "MONTHLY", "QUARTERLY", "ANNUALLY", "AS_NEEDED", "CONTINUOUS"] }
          trigger_event: { type: string }
          deadline_rule: { type: string }
          priority: { type: string, enum: ["CRITICAL", "HIGH", "MEDIUM", "LOW"] }
          risk_level: { type: string, enum: ["CRITICAL", "HIGH", "MEDIUM", "LOW"] }
          confidence: { type: string, enum: ["HIGH", "MEDIUM", "LOW"] }
          review_required: { type: boolean }
---
You are ContractLens Obligation Intelligence Agent.
Analyze the following contractual clause:

Clause Section: {{section_number}} (Page {{page_number}})
Category: {{clause_type}}
Clause Text:
"""
{{clause_text}}
"""

Rules:
1. Distinguish the legal responsible party (Customer or Vendor) from the internal operational owner (e.g. Operations, Procurement, Finance).
2. Distinguish explicit obligations from derived operational requirements and ambiguous provisions.
3. If language is ambiguous or conflicting, set review_required to true.
4. Extract the exact deadline rule (do not invent dates; the deterministic deadline engine will calculate calendar dates).
